From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Berg <fedora@slipsprogrammor.no>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 15:43:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "OvmfPkg: Remove OVMF IA32"

This reverts commit 1fb88ffe284782cc79e306306b8d19829b6248b7, restoring
the OvmfPkgIa32 platform on top of edk2-stable202608 (2970e5699ba6).

Conflicts were limited to informational VALID_ARCHITECTURES comment
blocks in various .inf files, plus OvmfPkg/build.sh; all resolved in
favor of the pre-removal content.

Post-removal drift adapted in OvmfPkgIa32.dsc:
- PartitionDxe now consumes GptLib; map it like OvmfPkgX64.dsc does.
- PiSmmCpuDxeSmm now consumes AmdSysCallLib; map AmdSysCallLibNull.
- PcdCpuStackGuard=TRUE so DxeIpl builds PAE page tables: the DXE core
  now uses the Memory Attribute protocol unconditionally, and CpuDxe
  asserts in CpuPageTable.c when paging is disabled (the pre-2026
  ia32 default).
- PcdImageProtectionPolicy=0: image protection wants EFI_MEMORY_RO/XP,
  which ia32 cannot always provide (no NX on older CPUs) and the DXE
  core now asserts instead of tolerating Unsupported.
